## Overall layout

* The web app uses a left=E2=80=91hand navigation bar with icons for the ma=
in modules. Hovering over each icon reveals labels for **Dashboard**, **Obj=
ekte (Properties)**, **Mietverh=C3=A4ltnisse (Tenancies)**, **Z=C3=A4hler (=
Meters)**, **Betriebskosten (Operating=E2=80=91cost statements)**, **Kontak=
te (Contacts)**, **Miet=C3=BCbersicht (Rent overview)**, **Finanzen/Banking=
**, **Nachrichten (Messages)**, **Dokumente (Documents)** and profile setti=
ngs.
* A trial banner at the top shows how many days remain in the test period a=
nd links to upgrade to a paid plan.

## Properties (Objekte)

* The *Objekte* page lists all properties with columns for the number of un=
its, total area, property category and rent balance. Each row shows address=
 details and indicates overdue rent in red. Filters allow searching by name=
, payment status or specific objects.
* Clicking a property opens a detailed view. The =E2=80=9CHaus Hafencity=E2=
=80=9D page illustrates typical data: key figures such as cold rent, rent p=
er square metre and floor area; a photo; a map; and sections for contacts (=
owner, property manager, etc.).
* The overview includes a rent ledger for each unit showing due/paid rent a=
nd balances, a list of units with their status (rented/vacant), and cards f=
or uploading documents and taking notes.

## Units &amp; Tenancies

* In the *Mietverh=C3=A4ltnisse* module, a dashboard summarises the number =
of total, rented, terminated, vacant and reserved tenancies. A table lists =
each unit, its tenant and status, with quick actions to view or edit the te=
nancy.
* Clicking a tenancy opens the unit=E2=80=99s detail page where you can see=
 living area, cold rent, equipment features (e.g. cellar, guest WC), tenanc=
y start date and terms. It also displays a rent ledger, the current tenant=
=E2=80=99s contact and bank details, notes and messaging history.

## Utility meters and operating costs

* The *Z=C3=A4hler* page lets you manage utility meters. A table (empty in =
the test account) would show meter numbers, associated units, last readings=
, consumption period and supplier. There is a button to add new meters and =
export data.
* *Betriebskostenabrechnungen* provides tools to create annual service=E2=
=80=91charge statements. Filters select objects and statuses, and buttons a=
llow creating a new statement or copying one from the previous year.

## Contacts &amp; Communication

* *Kontakte* holds all contacts (tenants, owners, suppliers etc.). Entries =
display contact details, address, phone numbers and roles. You can filter b=
y contact type and export contacts, and a button adds new contacts.
* Opening a contact shows two tabs: *Kontaktdetails* (email, phone, assigne=
d properties, bank details, creditor/debtor IDs) and *Finanzdetails*. From =
here you can edit information, send messages or add notes.
* *Nachrichten* acts as a messaging inbox. Currently there are no conversat=
ions in the test account, but the interface allows starting new conversatio=
ns and would list message threads once active.

## Rent overview and finances

* The *Miet=C3=BCbersicht* module is a central rent ledger. It lists each t=
enant with their object, rent month (=E2=80=9CMiete&nbsp;3/2026=E2=80=9D et=
c.), payment status (Open/Overdue/Paid) and amount. Filters allow searching=
 by tenant name, object, owner, time period and payment status; data can be=
 exported.
* The *Bankkonten* page connects bank accounts to automatically import tran=
sactions. In the test account no bank is linked, but the page shows tabs fo=
r all transactions, suggestions, unassigned transactions and ignored entrie=
s. There is a button to connect a bank and functions to automatically match=
 payments to rents.
* An overall *Finanzen* section (accessible via property/unit pages) summar=
ises income/expenses and allows recording costs or revenues manually.

## Documents

* The *Dokumente* area contains an inbox and folders for each property. You=
 can upload documents (max 25&nbsp;MB) via drag=E2=80=91and=E2=80=91drop an=
d search by date or keyword. The system also provides a personal immocloud =
email address to forward documents directly into the inbox for later proces=
sing.

## Additional features

* A *Z=C3=A4hler* icon in the left navigation reveals tools for managing ut=
ility meters.
* A small profile avatar at the bottom opens a menu for settings, help, ref=
errals and logout.
* The platform also supports integration with advertising portals such as I=
mmobilienScout24 (button =E2=80=9CIS24 Expos=C3=A9 erstellen=E2=80=9D) when=
 editing units.

**Summary:** Immocloud is an all=E2=80=91in=E2=80=91one property=E2=80=91ma=
nagement platform designed for landlords. Its modular navigation provides a=
ccess to property and unit details, rent tracking, tenant contracts, meter =
readings, service=E2=80=91charge statements, contact management, banking in=
tegration, messaging and document management. The UI is coherent, with filt=
erable tables, clear status indicators (e.g. overdue rents), and integratio=
n points for bank accounts and external marketing portals.
