<h2 data-section-id=3D"18flha2" data-start=3D"7162" data-end=3D"7232">Sympt=
om: CSV/XLSX/PDF downloads fail in browser, but work in <code data-start=3D=
"7226" data-end=3D"7232">curl</code></h2>
<p data-start=3D"7234" data-end=3D"7316">Then the backend is usually fine a=
nd the problem is in the frontend download path.</p>
<p data-start=3D"7318" data-end=3D"7343">Check whether the client:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"7344" data-end=3D"7486">
<li data-section-id=3D"1m67eun" data-start=3D"7344" data-end=3D"7381">
<p data-start=3D"7346" data-end=3D"7381">tries to parse the response as JSO=
N</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"qpnp3o" data-start=3D"7382" data-end=3D"7398">
<p data-start=3D"7384" data-end=3D"7398">loses the Blob</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"rmtr3k" data-start=3D"7399" data-end=3D"7441">
<p data-start=3D"7401" data-end=3D"7441">fails to call <code data-start=3D"=
7415" data-end=3D"7441">URL.createObjectURL(...)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"12s2vhv" data-start=3D"7442" data-end=3D"7486">
<p data-start=3D"7444" data-end=3D"7486">uses the wrong filename/content ty=
pe logic</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"7488" data-end=3D"7658">The backend side is valid as long =
as the route returns the correct content type and body; the renderer should=
 branch for binary responses instead of always assuming JSON.</p>
<h2 data-section-id=3D"133y7u9" data-start=3D"7660" data-end=3D"7713">Sympt=
om: rent-charge generation creates duplicates</h2>
<p data-start=3D"7715" data-end=3D"7829">The generator needs an idempotency=
 check on <code data-start=3D"7759" data-end=3D"7780">(tenancy_id, month)</=
code> before inserting. If duplicates appear, inspect:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"7831" data-end=3D"7925">
<li data-section-id=3D"1nxpq4l" data-start=3D"7831" data-end=3D"7852">
